{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nfrom sys import stdin\nimport sys\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10 ** 6)\n\nn, k = map(int, stdin.readline().strip().split())\nMOD = 10 ** 9 + 7\n\nadj = [-1] * (n + 1)\nfor i in range(n):\n    adj[i] = (i * k) % n\n\nvisited = [False] * (n + 1)\n\ndef mark(start):\n    u = start\n    while not visited[u]:\n        visited[u] = True\n        u = adj[u]\n\npairs = 0\nfor i in range(1, n):\n    if not visited[i]:\n        mark(i)\n        pairs += 1\n\nif k == 1:\n    print(pow(n, n, MOD))\nelse:\n    print(pow(n, pairs, MOD))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int k = sc.nextInt();\n        final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n\n        int[] adj = new int[n + 1];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            adj[i] = (i * k) % n;\n        }\n        adj[n] = -1; // not strictly needed, but matches original\n\n        boolean[] visited = new boolean[n + 1];\n\n        // mark function as iterative\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n            if (!visited[i]) {\n                int u = i;\n                while (!visited[u]) {\n                    visited[u] = true;\n                    u = adj[u];\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // count pairs: number of times we started a new mark (i.e., number of components)\n        // Actually we need to count the number of times we called mark, which is the number of unvisited nodes in the loop.\n        // But we already did the marking in the loop above. We need to count the number of starts.\n        // Let's recount properly.\n        // Reset visited? No, we need to count pairs as in original: for i in 1..n-1, if not visited, mark and pairs++.\n        // So we need to do the marking and counting simultaneously.\n        // We'll redo with counting.\n        visited = new boolean[n + 1]; // reset\n        int pairs = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n            if (!visited[i]) {\n                pairs++;\n                int u = i;\n                while (!visited[u]) {\n                    visited[u] = true;\n                    u = adj[u];\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        long result;\n        if (k == 1) {\n            result = modPow(n, n, MOD);\n        } else {\n            result = modPow(n, pairs, MOD);\n        }\n        System.out.println(result);\n        sc.close();\n    }\n\n    private static long modPow(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long result = 1;\n        base %= mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.3828182090946939e-05, -2.5033